Every buprenorphine carries a less-than-full-agonist-overdose-likelihood.
If a patient takes a buprenorphine then a buprenorphine-overdose can possibly occur for the patient.
If a patient concurrently takes a buprenorphine and concurrently takes an other-respiratory-depressant then a buprenorphine-overdose can particularly occur for the patient.
An other-respiratory-depressant-example includes a full-agonist-opioid-example and includes a benzodiazepine-example and includes an alcohol-example.
